---
title: Diagrama de clases inicial (revisión 1200e73)
---
classDiagram
    direction TB

    class BaseModel {
        <<pydantic>>
    }
    class FastAPI {
        <<FastAPI>>
        +state.database: Database
    }
    class HTTPException {
        <<FastAPI>>
        +status_code: int
        +detail: str
    }
    class Connection {
        <<sqlite3>>
    }

    class Database {
        +path: str
        +connect() Iterator~Connection~
        +initialize() None
    }

    class ProductInput {
        +name: str
        +price_cents: int
        +stock: int
    }
    class CustomerInput {
        +name: str
        +email: EmailStr
        +category: Literal["regular", "premium", "business"]
    }
    class ItemInput {
        +product_id: int
        +quantity: int
    }
    class OrderInput {
        +customer_id: int
        +address: str
        +city: str
        +postal_code: str
        +shipping: Literal["pickup", "standard", "express"]
        +items: list~ItemInput~
        +unique_products() OrderInput
    }

    class OrderService {
        +database: Database
        +save(customer_id, address, city, postal_code, shipping, items, order_id=None) dict
        +quote(data: OrderInput) dict
        +get(order_id) dict
        +list() list~dict~
        +confirm(order_id) dict
        +cancel(order_id) dict
        +delete(order_id) None
        +notifications(order_id) list~dict~
    }

    BaseModel <|-- ProductInput
    BaseModel <|-- CustomerInput
    BaseModel <|-- ItemInput
    BaseModel <|-- OrderInput
    OrderInput *-- "1..100" ItemInput : items

    FastAPI --> "1" Database : state.database
    OrderService --> "1" Database : database
    Database ..> Connection : abre y confirma
    OrderService ..> Connection : SQL sobre 5 tablas
    OrderService ..> OrderInput : quote(data)
    OrderService ..> ItemInput : save(items)
    OrderService ..> HTTPException : lanza 404 / 409

    note for OrderService "save() crea si order_id es None y edita si no.<br>save() y quote() repiten el cálculo de descuento y envío.<br>SQL sobre orders, order_items, customers, products y notifications.<br>Las rutas de app/orders.py crean un OrderService por petición."
    note for Database "Las rutas de app/products.py y app/customers.py<br>usan Database directamente (no hay clase de servicio)."
